    content: "---\nname: play-policy\ndescription: >\n  Provides guidance and compliant implementation patterns for Google Play Developer Program policies.\n  Use when selecting Android permissions, designing media selection flows, or choosing foreground services and execution architectures.\n---\n\n# Google Play Policy Compliance\n\nGuidelines, prohibited anti-patterns, and compliant code implementations to\nensure Android apps adhere to Google Play Developer Program policies.\n\n## Policy Reference Index\n\n-   **Permissions & APIs**\n    ([permissions_and_apis.md](references/permissions_and_apis.md)): Photo\n    Picker over storage permissions, location access constraints, and restricted\n    permissions.\n-   **App Metadata & Branding** ([app_metadata.md](references/app_metadata.md)):\n    Title $\\le 30$ chars, no emojis/ALL CAPS/buzzwords, and anti-impersonation.\n-   **System Integrity**\n    ([system_integrity.md](references/system_integrity.md)): Prohibition on\n    Dynamic Code Loading (DCL) and explicit `foregroundServiceType`\n    declarations.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Core Development Rules\n\n1.  **Permissions Minimization**: Never request broad permissions when\n    zero-permission alternatives (Photo Picker, SAF, standard Intents) exist.\n2.  **Clean Metadata**: Keep app titles $\\le 30$ characters and free of emojis,\n    all-caps, or promotional claims.\n3.  **No Dynamic Execution**: Never download and execute external `.dex`,\n    `.jar`, or `.so` files at runtime.\n"
    num_lines: 36
    num_bytes: 1524
    is_skill_file: true
    skill_metadata {
      name: "play-policy"
      description: "Provides guidance and compliant implementation patterns for Google Play Developer Program policies. Use when selecting Android permissions, designing media selection flows, or choosing foreground services and execution architectures."
    }
