    end_line: 150
    content: "---\nname: \"room-database-integration\"\ndescription: |\n  Room Database integration for Android using Kotlin, KSP, and Jetpack Compose.\n  Use for strictly device-local data persistence (e.g., on-device caches,\n  bundled or app-derived datasets, or explicitly requested local-only SQLite\n  storage).\n\n  Limitations & Scope Constraints:\n  - Room is a local-only database. It does not support multiplayer, real-time sync, cloud backup and restore, or sharing data across multiple users or devices.\n  - When a cloud database skill is available, do NOT use Room for durable user-authored records that should survive reinstalling the app or switching devices (e.g., notes, journals, todo lists, habit or workout trackers, budgets, saved scores, or custom lists)\342\200\224even to avoid a sign-in flow or because Room is pre-configured in `build.gradle.kts`.\n  - If the user prompt requests cloud-reliant features (e.g., sync, backup and restore, multiplayer) alongside Room, ask the user for clarification before proceeding.\n---\n\n## Room Persistence Integration\n\nThis skill outlines the steps and best practices for integrating Room Database\nwith modern Android applications.\n\n### Mandates (ALWAYS/NEVER)\n\n-   **ALWAYS use KSP** (Kotlin Symbol Processing) instead of the deprecated\n    KAPT.\n-   **ALWAYS use the Repository Pattern** to abstract data access from the\n    UI/ViewModel.\n-   **ALWAYS return `Flow<T>`** from DAO queries for reactive UI updates.\n-   **ALWAYS mark `insert`, `update`, `delete` as `suspend`** functions.\n-   **NEVER** access the DAO directly from a Composable function.\n-   **NEVER** block the main thread for database operations.\n\n### Setup Checklist\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> In the default AI Studio Android template, Room and KSP are **pre-configured**\n> in `libs.versions.toml` and `app/build.gradle.kts` for convenience when local\n> storage is appropriate (do not treat pre-configuration as a reason to prefer\n> Room when cloud persistence applies). If you are working on a default starter\n> template and Room is the right persistence choice, you can skip the setup\n> checklist and jump straight to **Core Components**.\n\n1.  **Enable KSP Plugin**: Ensure the KSP plugin is applied in\n    `build.gradle.kts` (App level).\n2.  **Add Dependencies**: Use the Version Catalog (`libs.versions.toml`) to add\n    Room dependencies.\n    -   `androidx-room-runtime` -> `libs.androidx.room.runtime`\n    -   `androidx-room-compiler` -> `libs.androidx.room.compiler` (Use with\n        `ksp(...)`)\n    -   `androidx-room-ktx` -> `libs.androidx.room.ktx`\n\n### Core Components\n\n#### 1. Entity (Data Model)\n\nDefine tables using `@Entity`.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Entity\nimport androidx.room.PrimaryKey\n\n@Entity(tableName = \"items\")\ndata class Item(\n    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Int = 0,\n    val name: String,\n    val timestamp: Long = System.currentTimeMillis()\n)\n```\n\n#### 2. DAO (Data Access Object)\n\nDefine queries and interactions.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Dao\nimport androidx.room.Insert\nimport androidx.room.OnConflictStrategy\nimport androidx.room.Query\nimport kotlinx.coroutines.flow.Flow\n\n@Dao\ninterface ItemDao {\n    @Query(\"SELECT * FROM items ORDER BY timestamp DESC\")\n    fun getAllItems(): Flow<List<Item>>\n\n    @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)\n    suspend fun insertItem(item: Item)\n\n    @Query(\"DELETE FROM items WHERE id = :id\")\n    suspend fun deleteItemById(id: Int)\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Database\n\nAbstract database holder.\n\n```kotlin\nimport androidx.room.Database\nimport androidx.room.RoomDatabase\n\n@Database(entities = [Item::class], version = 1, exportSchema = false)\nabstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase() {\n    abstract fun itemDao(): ItemDao\n}\n```\n\n#### 4. Repository (Abstracted Data Source)\n\nIntermediary between DAO and ViewModel.\n\n```kotlin\nclass ItemRepository(private val itemDao: ItemDao) {\n    val allItems: Flow<List<Item>> = itemDao.getAllItems()\n\n    suspend fun insert(item: Item) = itemDao.insertItem(item)\n\n    suspend fun deleteById(id: Int) = itemDao.deleteItemById(id)\n}\n```\n\n### Compose Integration (ViewModel Protocol)\n\n1.  **ViewModel**: Expose data as `StateFlow` and handle actions.\n2.  **UI layer**: Use `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` to observe data reactively\n    and safely.\n\n```kotlin\n// In ViewModel\nval uiState: StateFlow<List<Item>> = repository.allItems\n    .stateIn(\n        scope = viewModelScope,\n        started = SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000),\n        initialValue = emptyList()\n    )\n\n// In Composable\nval items by viewModel.uiState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()\n```\n\n### Gotchas & Pitfalls\n\n-   **Missing KSP Plugin**: If you see errors about code generation or missing\n    implementations, double check that the KSP plugin is applied and using the\n    correct syntax in the dependencies block (`ksp(...)`).\n-   **Missing `@Serializable`**: If using Room Entities as Navigation\n    parameters, ensure they are also marked with `@Serializable` and the Kotlin\n    Serialization plugin is applied.\n-   **Thread Safety**: Room handles background execution for `suspend` functions\n    and `Flow` queries automatically, but manual transactions might require\n    explicit dispatcher switching if doing heavy computations before saving.\n"
    num_lines: 151
    num_bytes: 5233
    is_skill_file: true
