  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/image-generation/SKILL.md"
    end_line: 107
    content: "---\nname: \"image-generation\"\ndescription: >-\n  Generates static pre-bundled UI drawable assets at build time (hero banners,\n  onboarding illustrations, backgrounds, avatars, placeholder photos) saved to\n  `res/drawable/`. Use when adding static visual UI polish or bundled artwork\n  to an Android app. Don\'t use for user-requested runtime AI image generation,\n  photo editing, or style remixing inside the app. For launcher icons, use\n  `app-icon-generation` instead.\n---\n\n# Images\n\n## When To Generate\n\n-   **Hero images, splash art, featured banners** \342\200\224 These set the tone for the\n    entire app.\n-   **Onboarding / empty-state illustrations** \342\200\224 Provide visual context when\n    there is no user data to display.\n-   **Card backgrounds and decorative elements** \342\200\224 Add depth and personality to\n    list items, detail screens, and headers.\n-   **Placeholder content** \342\200\224 For recipe images, travel destinations, product\n    photos, etc., generate thematically appropriate images rather than leaving\n    screens empty.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> **Generation Limit**: Limit calls to `generate_image` to a maximum of **5\n> images per app**, unless more are explicitly requested by the user. There is a\n> strict limit to the number of images that can be generated per day per user\n> when using the free tier.\n\n## Implementation\n\nReference generated images saved as drawable resources directly:\n\n```kotlin\nImage(\n    painter = painterResource(id = R.drawable.img_hero_banner),\n    contentDescription = \"Hero banner\",\n    modifier = Modifier.fillMaxWidth(),\n    contentScale = ContentScale.Crop\n)\n```\n\n### Output Location\n\nThe `generate_image` tool saves images as either `.jpg` or `.png` files,\ndepending on the image model\'s MIME type \342\200\224 do not assume the extension is\n`.png`. When generating images for an Android project, they are saved to\n`app/src/main/res/drawable/`. Name them with an `img_` prefix (e.g.,\n`img_hero_banner`, `img_profile_avatar`). For the app\'s **launcher icon**,\nalways follow the `app-icon-generation` skill (which configures adaptive vector\ndrawables in `ic_launcher_foreground.xml` / `ic_launcher_background.xml` and\nlegacy PNGs in `res/mipmap-*/`) rather than leaving a standalone drawable in\n`res/drawable/`.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n>\n> Avoid using the same name as existing XML drawables. For example, do not name\n> a generated asset `ic_launcher_foreground` if `ic_launcher_foreground.xml`\n> already exists, as this will cause duplicate resource errors.\n\n## Image Configuration\n\n-   `aspectRatio`: Changes the aspect ratio of the generated image. Supported\n    values are \"1:1\", \"3:4\", \"4:3\", \"9:16\", and \"16:9\", \"1:4\", \"1:8\", \"4:1\",\n    \"8:1\". The default is \"1:1\".\n\n### Aspect Ratio Selection\n\nChoose aspect ratio based on where the image will be used:\n\n-   **Hero / banner**: `16:9`\n-   **Card thumbnail**: `4:3`\n-   **Avatar / profile / App Icon**: `1:1`\n-   **Full-screen portrait (splash)**: `9:16`\n-   **Tall illustrative art**: `3:4`\n\n## Error Handling\n\n-   **Quota / Resource Exhausted**: If you encounter `resource_exhausted` or\n    `quota exceeded` errors when using `generate_image`, **do not** retry more\n    than once. Instead, inform the user that they have hit their free tier quota\n    for the day for generating images.\n\n## Edit Images\n\n-   To edit images using the tool, you can prompt with text, images, or a\n    combination of both.\n\n## Prompt Guidelines\n\nWrite detailed, descriptive prompts for better image quality:\n\n-   **Be specific**: \"A serene mountain landscape at golden hour with\n    snow-capped peaks reflected in a still alpine lake, photorealistic\" \342\200\224 not\n    \"mountain\".\n-   **Include style**: photorealistic, watercolor, flat design, 3D render,\n    minimalist, isometric, line art, pixel art, etc.\n-   **Specify composition**: close-up, wide-angle, bird\'s-eye view, centered,\n    rule-of-thirds, negative space.\n-   **Match the app\'s theme**: if the app uses a dark theme with neon accents,\n    describe that. If it\'s playful and colorful, reflect that in the prompt.\n-   **Context-appropriate**: hero banners should be expansive landscapes or\n    abstract patterns; card images should focus on a single subject; avatars\n    should be portraits or icons.\n"
    num_lines: 108
    num_bytes: 4207
    is_skill_file: true
    skill_metadata {
      name: "image-generation"
      description: "Generates static pre-bundled UI drawable assets at build time (hero banners, onboarding illustrations, backgrounds, avatars, placeholder photos) saved to `res/drawable/`. Use when adding static visual UI polish or bundled artwork to an Android app. Don\'t use for user-requested runtime AI image generation, photo editing, or style remixing inside the app. For launcher icons, use `app-icon-generation` instead."
    }
    line_range_bytes: 4207
  }
