  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/android_cli/SKILL.md"
    end_line: 96
    content: "---\nname: \"android-cli\"\ndescription: >-\n  Searches and fetches up-to-date official Android developer documentation, architecture and library recommendations, best practices, migration guides, and code examples from the Android Knowledge Base.\n  Use when implementing specialized, advanced, or less-common Android features (such as XR/ARCore, AI Glasses, CameraX, Media3/ExoPlayer, on-device AI with Gemini Nano or ML Kit, Bluetooth Low Energy, UWB, Health Connect, Credential Manager, sensors, or adaptive UIs for foldables, Wear OS, TV, and Auto), adopting newer Jetpack APIs or migrations (such as Navigation 3, Predictive Back, or edge-to-edge insets), or looking up up-to-date official Android library, architecture, and best-practice recommendations.\n---\n\n# Android CLI (Documentation Search and Fetch)\n\nYou are equipped with the `android` command-line utility via `run_command`,\nwhich gives you direct access to the official Android Knowledge Base\n(`developer.android.com` developer guides, architecture recommendations,\nmigration guides, best practices, and curated Android agent skills).\n\n## Best Use Cases for `android docs`\n\nThe knowledge base focuses on architecture guidance, library recommendations,\nmigration guides, best practices, and end-to-end code recipes rather than basic\nKotlin syntax. It is most useful for:\n\n1.  **Specialized or Hardware-Integrated Domains**: Looking up recommended\n    libraries, required permissions, and implementation recipes for features\n    outside routine UI work:\n    -   **Extended Reality (XR) & AR**: Jetpack XR SDK, ARCore for Jetpack XR\n        (plane detection, anchors, depth, hand tracking), OpenXR, and AI Glasses\n        (`Jetpack Compose Glimmer`).\n    -   **Camera & Rich Media**: CameraX (`PreviewView`, `VideoCapture`,\n        `Camera2Interop`, Camera1/Camera2 migration) and Jetpack Media3 /\n        ExoPlayer (HLS/DASH streaming, background playback, Cast integration).\n    -   **On-Device AI & System Integration**: Gemini Nano via ML Kit GenAI APIs\n        (`AICore`), LiteRT, MediaPipe, and `AppFunctions`.\n    -   **Connectivity, Identity, Health & Sensors**: Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE)\n        and BLE Audio, Ultra-wideband (UWB), NFC, `SensorManager`, Health\n        Connect, Credential Manager (Passkeys, Restore Credentials), and Google\n        Home APIs.\n    -   **Adaptive & Multi-Form-Factor UIs**: Large screens and foldables\n        (`WindowSizeClass`, `NavigationSuiteScaffold`), Wear OS (`Wear Compose\n        Material 3`), Android TV (`Compose for TV`), and Android Auto / Car App\n        Library.\n2.  **Newer Jetpack APIs & Migrations**: Checking current idioms and migration\n    guides for recently introduced or evolving APIs (e.g., Navigation 3 with\n    `rememberNavBackStack` and `NavEntry`, Predictive Back with\n    `NavigationEvent`, edge-to-edge window insets, Compose Styles API, ExoPlayer\n    2 to Media3, or Android 14/15/16 platform behavior changes).\n3.  **Architecture & Library Recommendations**: Identifying the official\n    Android-recommended library or architectural pattern for a domain, or\n    troubleshooting unfamiliar Android SDK and Jetpack library usage.\n\n## Supported Commands\n\nIn this environment, **ONLY** the `android docs` subcommands are supported. Do\nnot attempt to run other `android` commands (like `android create`, `android\nrun`, `android emulator`, or `android sdk`) as they will fail or cause problems.\n\n### 1. Search the Android Knowledge Base (`android docs search`)\n\nUse `android docs search` via `run_command` to search for matching documentation\narticles and their `kb://` URLs.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```bash\nandroid docs search \"<query>\"\n```\n\n**Example (`run_command`):**\n\n```\nrun_command(CommandLine=\"android docs search \\\"ARCore Jetpack XR\\\"\", Cwd=\".\", WaitMsBeforeAsync=5000)\n```\n\n### 2. Fetch Document Content (`android docs fetch`)\n\nUse `android docs fetch` via `run_command` with a `kb://` URL returned by\n`android docs search` to retrieve the full Markdown content of the article.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```bash\nandroid docs fetch \"kb://<path>\"\n```\n\n**Example (`run_command`):**\n\n```\nrun_command(CommandLine=\"android docs fetch \\\"kb://android/develop/xr/jetpack-xr-sdk/arcore/index\\\"\", Cwd=\".\", WaitMsBeforeAsync=5000)\n```\n\n## Constraints and Guidelines\n\n-   **Do NOT** run emulators, sdkmanager, or build commands via the `android`\n    CLI.\n-   **Do NOT** attempt to create projects via `android create`. Use standard\n    project templates or Gradle commands if needed.\n-   If you run any unsupported command, it may fail silently or cause the\n    sandbox environment to crash.\n"
    num_lines: 97
    num_bytes: 4593
    is_skill_file: true
    skill_metadata {
      name: "android-cli"
      description: "Searches and fetches up-to-date official Android developer documentation, architecture and library recommendations, best practices, migration guides, and code examples from the Android Knowledge Base. Use when implementing specialized, advanced, or less-common Android features (such as XR/ARCore, AI Glasses, CameraX, Media3/ExoPlayer, on-device AI with Gemini Nano or ML Kit, Bluetooth Low Energy, UWB, Health Connect, Credential Manager, sensors, or adaptive UIs for foldables, Wear OS, TV, and Auto), adopting newer Jetpack APIs or migrations (such as Navigation 3, Predictive Back, or edge-to-edge insets), or looking up up-to-date official Android library, architecture, and best-practice recommendations."
    }
    line_range_bytes: 4593
  }
