  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Core**\n\nI\'m digging into the user\'s prompt, focusing on its core meaning. It\'s clear that building an answering machine app on Android faces limitations, which means the development approach is key. I\'m focusing on the implied constraints and opportunities for realistic options.\n\n\n**Evaluating Android Options**\n\nI\'ve examined the Android options, particularly default dialer/InCallService apps. While they offer the most control (auto-answer, greeting), the call audio stream restrictions are a significant hurdle. I\'m noting the limited utility of speakerphone workarounds, and why rooted/custom ROM methods are not applicable. Considering CallScreeningService\'s limitations, I\'m now leaning toward the carrier voicemail route as most viable for the Google Play Store.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Cloud Integration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the cloud-based answering machine solution. The limitations of on-device recording are too restrictive. I\'m focusing on the cloud alternative, specifically a VoIP-forwarding approach for recording reliably. This seems like the most practical path, despite the added cost and backend complexity.\n\n\n"
