  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Installing Fonts Progress**\n\nI\'m pleased to report a successful installation of all three fonts: `space_grotesk.ttf`, `plus_jakarta_sans.ttf`, and `jetbrains_mono.ttf`. Moving forward, I\'ll be focused on generating the custom app launcher icon foreground image, `ic_launcher_art`. The `generate_image` function is next on the agenda and the save operation will be next on this list.\n\n\n**Clarifying Asset Location**\n\nI\'m now clarifying where `generate_image` saves its output. Initially, I was unsure whether it used `app/src/main/res/drawable/` or an artifact directory, but the `app-icon-generation` skill description confirms this destination. I\'m checking the `generate_image` tool\'s `ImageName` parameter and reviewing where generated assets are stored. I\'m ready to call the tool to create the launcher icon foreground.\n\n\n**Considering Asset Generation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on generating two assets in parallel: `img_deck_hero` (16:9) and a corresponding Answering Machine console illustration. The prompts are set. I need to update `metadata.json`, `settings.gradle.kts`, and `app/build.gradle.kts`. But, let me review `metadata.json` first, and then I will think further about persistence and Firebase.\n\n\n**Evaluating Persistence Strategies**\n\nI\'m now carefully re-reading the Core Data Persistence rules. The key question is whether Firebase Firestore is warranted. I am assessing if Firebase Firestore\'s persistence rules should apply, based on whether the data is critical or shared. I\'m focusing on the nature of data and if it needs cloud persistence, and then I\'ll finalize the choice, based on the `guidelines` content.\n\n\n**Analyzing Persistence Options**\n\nI\'ve re-read the Core Data Persistence rules and the user prompt\'s comparison of options. I can see I need an *on-device* answering machine with audio files and message metadata stored locally on the device, specifically with Room to manage metadata. I am confident Firebase Firestore is not needed here; my focus is now on the architecture, which is coming into view.\n\n\n**Confirming Data Storage**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data storage. I\'m confirming that DataStore is the correct place to store local answering machine settings, such as auto-answer enabled, rings before answer, and active greeting ID. Audio file paths will link to local `filesDir` locations, all on-device, alongside local telephony recordings. Room and DataStore are indeed the correct compliant storage choices. Now I can move on to asset generation. I plan to call `generate_image` for the icon foreground and hero artwork next.\n\n\n"
