    thinking: "**Designing Package Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the Kotlin package within `com.example`. I\'m starting with a `ui/theme/` package. Inside, I plan to create a `Color.kt` file. This will contain the tactile studio color palette, which includes Charcoal Slate for dark surfaces, Brushed Aluminum and Warm Ivory for light surfaces, and Signal Amber (#FF6B2B) for the primary color.\n\n\n**Refining Color and Typography**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Phosphor Emerald secondary, Amber Gold tertiary, and Crimson error colors into my design, adding depth to the palette. I\'ve also established my typography in `Type.kt`, using Space Grotesk, Plus Jakarta Sans, and JetBrains Mono. My `Theme.kt` is being crafted with custom shapes, color schemes, and defaulting `dynamicColor = false` for consistency. I am working on how the custom palette looks compared to default options.\n\n\n**Defining Data Layer Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the data layer components. I\'ve got `EchoDeckDao.kt` handling reactive queries and database operations using Flows and suspend functions. The database itself, `EchoDeckDatabase.kt`, is a singleton and includes initial TTS greetings, but only on an empty greetings table. Finally, `MachinePreferencesRepository.kt` uses DataStore for machine settings, while `EchoDeckRepository.kt` manages data interaction with the DAO and file storage.\n\n\n**Developing Audio Implementation**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the `audio/` package. I\'ve engineered a real Android audio engine. Specifically, `AudioRecorderController` records `.m4a` files using `MediaRecorder`, providing real-time `maxAmplitude` data with `StateFlow<Int>`. On the other hand, `AudioPlayerController` leverages `MediaPlayer` for playback with `StateFlow<PlaybackState>` and speakerphone/earpiece toggling. I\'ve included a `BeepGenerator`, avoiding raw files. Finally, there is the `TtsSpeaker` component.\n\n\n**Implementing Call Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the call handling services. The `EchoInCallService.kt` manages call lifecycles, full-screen notifications for incoming calls, and executes the auto-answer pipeline. When `isMachineEnabled` is true, or on user tap, it runs a countdown. It handles the whole sequence: answering, speakerphone, greeting playback (recorded or TTS), beep, recording via `MediaRecorder`, and saving a `VoicemailMessageEntity`. Then, it posts a \"New Voicemail\" notification. Also, I\'ve got a `EchoCallScreeningService.kt` up and running.\n\n\n**Defining Call Filtering & Application**\n\nI\'m now integrating call screening rules and application-level components. I\'ve defined `ScreeningRuleEntity` and a `screenUnknownCallers` preference, which will apply configured actions like `disallowCall`, `silenceCall`, or `skipCallLog`. The `CallActionReceiver.kt` now handles all notification intents such as answering, sending to the machine, and declining calls. In `SystemCapabilityHelper.kt`, I\'m verifying essential system capabilities. Finally, `EchoDeckApplication.kt` is established as the application class, housing singletons for core components like the database and audio engine, also creating notification channels during startup.\n\nI\'m focusing on the UI components now. I\'ve designed custom Compose Canvas components for `TapeVisuals.kt`, including an animated cassette reel indicator, a real-time VU meter, and a waveform visualizer, all in the `ui/` package.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in constructing UI components. I\'m focusing on `TapeVisuals.kt` for interactive waveform scrubbing using `waveformPeaks` and real-time peak arrays. I\'m creating the core screen layouts now. I have a deck console screen, an inbox, a greeting studio, and a dialer screen.\n\n\n**Designing App-Level Components**\n\nI\'m now designing the top-level app components and call screen features. I\'m focusing on key screens and rules. I\'m structuring `EchoDeckApp.kt` with a navigation scaffold and `@Serializable` routes. There is now a dedicated in-call HUD with several functions. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined data entities for rules and voicemail, and also built a new navigation.\n\n\n"
