    thinking: "**Refining Deletion Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed that deleting the active greeting requires updating which greeting is \"active\" next. I\'m leaning toward adding a `getMostRecentGreeting()` query to the DAO, but I need to quickly test the scenarios: What happens if there are two greetings? Three? What if it\'s the last greeting? It might require adding an explicit logic call to the repository and Dao.\n\n\n**Implementing Greeting Management**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing automatic active greeting selection after deletion. I\'m adding `getAnyGreeting()` to `EchoDeckDao` and calling it within `deleteGreeting`. This ensures a greeting is always active. I am excited to work in `AudioEngine.kt` and `SystemCapabilityHelper.kt`! I\'m carefully designing the `AudioEngine` with distinct states and player/recorder controllers.\n\n\n**Designing Audio Handling**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the audio handling logic. My initial focus is on the `MediaRecorder` setup, specifically the API level adaptations, using `MediaRecorder(context)` on newer versions and the standard constructor on older ones. I am excited to work on capturing the `AudioSource.MIC` input, potentially falling back to `VOICE_COMMUNICATION`. I\'m especially keen on the `maxAmplitude` polling and the waveform peak generation. I also want to work on `startRecording` and `stopRecording` functions.\n\n\n"
