  planner_response {
    response: "Built **EchoDeck**, an on-device Android answering machine and dialer application in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose using `InCallService`, `CallScreeningService`, `MediaRecorder`/`MediaPlayer`, DataStore, and Room.\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n- **Telephony & Auto-Answer Pipeline (`InCallService` & `CallScreeningService`)**\n  - Registered `EchoInCallService` (`BIND_INCALL_SERVICE` with `IN_CALL_SERVICE_UI` and `IN_CALL_SERVICE_RINGING`) and `ACTION_DIAL` / `tel:` intent handling so the app can hold `RoleManager.ROLE_DIALER`.\n  - Counts incoming rings based on the user-configured ring threshold, automatically answers with `VideoProfile.STATE_AUDIO_ONLY`, optionally switches to speakerphone for Android 10+ acoustic capture, plays the active greeting (recorded `.m4a` file or `TextToSpeech` script), emits a synthesized 980 Hz `AudioTrack` tone, and records the caller\'s audio message via `MediaRecorder` while sampling live waveform amplitudes.\n  - Added `EchoCallScreeningService` (`ROLE_CALL_SCREENING`) to evaluate incoming numbers against user-defined allow, direct-to-machine, and block rules, plus an optional unknown-caller blocker.\n  - Added `InCallActivity` and `NotificationHelper` for lockscreen-capable incoming call controls (**Answer**, **Send to Answering Machine Now**, **Decline**), live answering machine progress, DTMF keypad, mute/speaker toggles, and new voicemail alerts.\n\n- **Local Persistence (Room + DataStore)**\n  - **Room Database (`EchoDeckDatabase`)**: Stores `VoicemailMessageEntity` (caller metadata, duration, `.m4a` path, read/starred status, caller notes, and sampled waveform peaks), `GreetingEntity` (recorded audio or TTS script greetings with active selection), and `ScreeningRuleEntity`.\n  - **DataStore (`MachinePreferencesRepository`)**: Persists armed/standby status, rings before auto-answer (1\342\200\2238), max recording length (30s\342\200\223180s), speakerphone capture toggle, post-greeting tone toggle, and unknown-caller screening.\n\n- **Jetpack Compose UI (Adaptive Material 3)**\n  - **Deck Console**: Master armed switch, animated cassette reel canvas indicator, active greeting selector, live telephony role/permission readiness checklist (`RoleManager` and runtime permissions), pickup/capture controls, and a local **Acoustic Pipeline Verification** test to verify greeting playback, beep generation, and microphone recording end-to-end.\n  - **Tape Inbox**: Filterable voicemail list (`All`, `Unheard`, `Starred`) with inline `MediaPlayer` playback, tap-to-seek waveform scrubbing, speaker/earpiece routing, caller notes, audio `.m4a` sharing via `FileProvider`, callback, and delete.\n  - **Greeting Studio**: Record custom voice greetings with a live VU meter or create spoken TTS script greetings, preview takes, and switch active greetings.\n  - **Dialer & Screening**: Tactile DTMF keypad (`ToneGenerator` + `TelecomManager.placeCall`) paired with a number screening rule manager.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified the complete Android project build via `compile_applet` (build succeeded)."
    thinking: "**Awaiting Task Completion**\n\nI\'m currently paused, awaiting the completion message from `task-89`. It\'s a `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` background process. I need to know if it finished successfully before I can proceed with the next steps, or perhaps consider alternative tooling strategies. I\'m focusing on managing this task dependency. Let\'s monitor the `manage_task` system and wait.\n\n\n**Clarifying Task Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve realized I was incorrectly assuming a polling strategy, which is against instructions. I need to be patient. I was confused, since a previous tool call waited for `task-89` (or ran after) to succeed. My `compile_applet` tool ran with `waitForPreviousTools: true`, and it completed successfully at `04:38:37`. I\'m going to check the `manage_task(Action=\"list\")` one last time, to see if `task-89` already finished, or view the test report, but not poll. I\'ll make a final, concise summary.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Built **EchoDeck**, an on-device Android answering machine and dialer application in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose using `InCallService`, `CallScreeningService`, `MediaRecorder`/`MediaPlayer`, DataStore, and Room.\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n- **Telephony & Auto-Answer Pipeline (`InCallService` & `CallScreeningService`)**\n  - Registered `EchoInCallService` (`BIND_INCALL_SERVICE` with `IN_CALL_SERVICE_UI` and `IN_CALL_SERVICE_RINGING`) and `ACTION_DIAL` / `tel:` intent handling so the app can hold `RoleManager.ROLE_DIALER`.\n  - Counts incoming rings based on the user-configured ring threshold, automatically answers with `VideoProfile.STATE_AUDIO_ONLY`, optionally switches to speakerphone for Android 10+ acoustic capture, plays the active greeting (recorded `.m4a` file or `TextToSpeech` script), emits a synthesized 980 Hz `AudioTrack` tone, and records the caller\'s audio message via `MediaRecorder` while sampling live waveform amplitudes.\n  - Added `EchoCallScreeningService` (`ROLE_CALL_SCREENING`) to evaluate incoming numbers against user-defined allow, direct-to-machine, and block rules, plus an optional unknown-caller blocker.\n  - Added `InCallActivity` and `NotificationHelper` for lockscreen-capable incoming call controls (**Answer**, **Send to Answering Machine Now**, **Decline**), live answering machine progress, DTMF keypad, mute/speaker toggles, and new voicemail alerts.\n\n- **Local Persistence (Room + DataStore)**\n  - **Room Database (`EchoDeckDatabase`)**: Stores `VoicemailMessageEntity` (caller metadata, duration, `.m4a` path, read/starred status, caller notes, and sampled waveform peaks), `GreetingEntity` (recorded audio or TTS script greetings with active selection), and `ScreeningRuleEntity`.\n  - **DataStore (`MachinePreferencesRepository`)**: Persists armed/standby status, rings before auto-answer (1\342\200\2238), max recording length (30s\342\200\223180s), speakerphone capture toggle, post-greeting tone toggle, and unknown-caller screening.\n\n- **Jetpack Compose UI (Adaptive Material 3)**\n  - **Deck Console**: Master armed switch, animated cassette reel canvas indicator, active greeting selector, live telephony role/permission readiness checklist (`RoleManager` and runtime permissions), pickup/capture controls, and a local **Acoustic Pipeline Verification** test to verify greeting playback, beep generation, and microphone recording end-to-end.\n  - **Tape Inbox**: Filterable voicemail list (`All`, `Unheard`, `Starred`) with inline `MediaPlayer` playback, tap-to-seek waveform scrubbing, speaker/earpiece routing, caller notes, audio `.m4a` sharing via `FileProvider`, callback, and delete.\n  - **Greeting Studio**: Record custom voice greetings with a live VU meter or create spoken TTS script greetings, preview takes, and switch active greetings.\n  - **Dialer & Screening**: Tactile DTMF keypad (`ToneGenerator` + `TelecomManager.placeCall`) paired with a number screening rule manager.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified the complete Android project build via `compile_applet` (build succeeded)."
