  planner_response {
    response: "Fixed the GitHub Actions failure (`Error: Process completed with exit code 1`) and configured CI to build and upload the debug APK:\n\n### Cause\n- In `.github/workflows/detekt.yml`, the GraphQL query referenced `.data.repository.release.releaseAssets.tagCommit.oid` (which is `null` because `tagCommit` belongs on `release`, not `releaseAssets`), causing the SHA verification step to exit with code `1`. It also used Detekt `v1.15.0` (which predates Kotlin 2.2) and redirected `jq` output onto the same input file, truncating the SARIF report.\n- In `.github/workflows/blank.yml`, there was no Gradle/Android build setup, and on a fresh CI runner `debug.keystore` (which is gitignored) must be generated before `assembleDebug` runs.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n- **`.github/workflows/detekt.yml`**: Switched to JDK 17 with `detekt-cli` `1.23.8`, fixed the `jq` temporary-file write before `mv`, and added `security-events: write` permissions for SARIF upload.\n- **`.github/workflows/blank.yml`**: Configured JDK 17 and Gradle `9.3.1` (`gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v4`), added automatic `debug.keystore` generation if missing, runs `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` and `gradle :app:assembleDebug`, and uploads `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` as the **`EchoDeck-debug-apk`** workflow artifact.\n\nPush these updated workflow files to `main` (or trigger **Run workflow** manually from the GitHub **Actions** tab) to download the built APK from the run\'s **Artifacts** section."
    thinking: "**Verifying Secret Configurations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `blank.yml` file, cross-referencing it with the `app/build.gradle.kts` file\'s secrets plugin. Specifically, I\'m checking the `.env` and `.env.example` configurations, and double-checking the ignore list for any lingering `FIREBASE_` entries.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Fixed the GitHub Actions failure (`Error: Process completed with exit code 1`) and configured CI to build and upload the debug APK:\n\n### Cause\n- In `.github/workflows/detekt.yml`, the GraphQL query referenced `.data.repository.release.releaseAssets.tagCommit.oid` (which is `null` because `tagCommit` belongs on `release`, not `releaseAssets`), causing the SHA verification step to exit with code `1`. It also used Detekt `v1.15.0` (which predates Kotlin 2.2) and redirected `jq` output onto the same input file, truncating the SARIF report.\n- In `.github/workflows/blank.yml`, there was no Gradle/Android build setup, and on a fresh CI runner `debug.keystore` (which is gitignored) must be generated before `assembleDebug` runs.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n- **`.github/workflows/detekt.yml`**: Switched to JDK 17 with `detekt-cli` `1.23.8`, fixed the `jq` temporary-file write before `mv`, and added `security-events: write` permissions for SARIF upload.\n- **`.github/workflows/blank.yml`**: Configured JDK 17 and Gradle `9.3.1` (`gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v4`), added automatic `debug.keystore` generation if missing, runs `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` and `gradle :app:assembleDebug`, and uploads `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk` as the **`EchoDeck-debug-apk`** workflow artifact.\n\nPush these updated workflow files to `main` (or trigger **Run workflow** manually from the GitHub **Actions** tab) to download the built APK from the run\'s **Artifacts** section."
